00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:45.990
{=2}Group of Foreign Cyberbrain Engineers on Flight 381 Assumed Dead

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:49.030
The issue is, why'd he do it?

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:50.960
Who is he, anyway?

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:57.590
Murasaka Tei, male, age 32.

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:01.230
A stockbroker with dual Japanese and American citizenship?

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:03.040
No criminal record.

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:04.490
His address is...

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.360
Damn, someone beat us?

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:22.390
I love my job!

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:24.950
You've got to be kidding me.

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:31.540
What?!

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:46.090
Stop right there!

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:53.630
Shit!

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:05.400
Hello!

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:10.110
Behave yourself.

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:21.400
This guy...

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:32.350
You mind telling me why an American agent beat us to the suspect's condo?

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:36.410
Because you moved too fast.

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:42.010
You'd already charged in by the time the report made it through Foreign Affairs to me.

00:05:42.010 --> 00:05:44.490
Blame the bureaucracy for that.

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:47.740
<i>Your</i> team failed to call me directly.

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:56.020
Why didn't you tell me you'd connected 
the attack on Flight 381 with Fire-Starter?

00:05:57.010 --> 00:05:58.580
The intel came through my personal Net.

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:00.780
I can't reveal my source.

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:03.550
I see. Then let's make a deal.

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:12.610
The man you were after, Murasaka Tei, isn't a stockbroker—he's an American intelligence agent.

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:13.970
Who told you that?

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:16.680
His colleague.

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:22.190
Murasaka is indeed an agent of ours.

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:26.280
Nice to meet you, Major Kusanagi.

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:29.200
I'm Jeril, with American Army intelligence.

00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:38.130
This is our recommended prosthetic body
 for diplomatic activities. Is there a problem?

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:39.550
None whatsoever.

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:48.650
Well? Have you been pursuing Fire-Starter's broker, too?

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:49.470
Yes.

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:53.680
We refer to him as "Pyromaniac,"

00:06:54.390 --> 00:07:00.430
because his virus sales unleash
 Fire-Starter damage wherever he goes.

00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:04.480
I'd love to have your help capturing him.

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:09.610
If you're looking to catch a firebug, 
aren't you asking the wrong department?

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:15.830
You're the only firefighter with a record of success against Fire-Starter.

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:21.670
I believe that makes you the perfect observer for our capture op.

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:23.290
What're the details of this op?

00:07:23.890 --> 00:07:30.530
Pyromaniac is in Japan right now to carry out a hit on Colonel Hozumi for the cartel.

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:37.290
Our antivirus specialist Murasaka was on his trail, but we abruptly lost contact.

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:44.230
And by the time you found him, he'd already been
 infected and made the terrorist attack on Flight 381.

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:48.680
Foreign Affairs passed along a request for a joint operation.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:51.580
You join in.

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:54.660
<i>My</i> team, under American Army command?

00:07:55.190 --> 00:07:57.120
The deal's already been done.

00:07:58.460 --> 00:07:59.440
Fine.

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:05.040
In exchange, I get to personally interrogate Hozumi and analyze the virus.

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:12.930
So you're telling us to join the fire brigade?

00:08:13.480 --> 00:08:15.660
When did you turn into a relief pitcher?

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:19.060
All we have to do is use the authority they gave us to beat them to him.

00:08:20.990 --> 00:08:24.330
We'll transfer Hozumi from the Army Medical Center to the courthouse.

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:27.880
The theory is that Pyromaniac will target her en route.

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:30.860
The Army's setting up an encirclement.

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:36.570
We'll anticipate the enemy's movements and stamp that fire out before it grows.

00:08:36.920 --> 00:08:38.830
We're firefighters now?!

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:41.890
And under Yankee coaching, too.

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:45.560
But once a game starts, it belongs to the players.

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:49.340
We'll be the ones to get Fire-Starter.

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:51.720
You plan to snatch their whole case?!

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:52.670
Problem?

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:57.220
Nah, I was getting sick of this dump anyway.

00:08:57.670 --> 00:09:02.320
Borma, you keep following up on the Flight 381 bombing.

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:05.090
Paz, go through Murasaka's background with a fine-tooth comb.

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:09.520
Ishikawa, look for data on Pyromaniac, and find out how he got Fire-Starter.

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:14.730
Batou, Togusa, and Saito,
 eliminate every possible way to hit Hozumi.

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:17.820
What'll <i>you</i> do?

00:09:19.430 --> 00:09:22.430
I'll get the bait we need to trap him.

00:09:38.270 --> 00:09:43.850
How does it feel to be nothing but a head, Colonel Hozumi?

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:46.850
The false signals aren't too bad.

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:49.440
I wouldn't call the experience pleasant, though.

00:09:49.960 --> 00:09:51.770
What brings you here?

00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:58.440
Your past ties to the cartel make you useful.

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:01.410
That's it? Just kill me.

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:06.800
Pyromaniac wants to get rid of the information in your brain.

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:10.290
You'll be our bait to lure him out.

00:10:10.810 --> 00:10:12.960
I'm a witness!

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:17.980
And as long as you stay within my sight and my reach, I'll protect you.

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:37.360
The negotiations are complete.

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:38.350
Understood.

00:10:38.350 --> 00:10:39.860
All as planned.

00:10:53.860 --> 00:11:02.300
Only by struggle and toil can we fulfill our duty,

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:06.920
and only information can bring true joy.

00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:45.810
I made the barriers around the facility nice and thick.

00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:49.730
We're sure to pick up on any data breach from outside.

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:53.200
Togusa here. I'm done checking out the transport route.

00:11:53.730 --> 00:11:55.470
No problems yet.

00:11:56.910 --> 00:12:00.010
I'm almost done marking the main sniper perches.

00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:03.610
Now it all depends on how good their snipers are.

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:05.330
Saito!

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:07.790
Where should we go next?

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:11.230
Wherever the wind blows, kid.

00:12:11.230 --> 00:12:12.560
Oh, wow!

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:14.930
Okay, I'll turn to windward!

00:12:17.300 --> 00:12:23.020
Listen, what if he gets inside disguised as a Public Security guy or a prosthetics tech?

00:12:23.020 --> 00:12:26.540
Hospital or not this is an Army facility.

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:29.270
You worry too much, rookie.

00:12:29.780 --> 00:12:34.100
Would we bother setting up a cordon like this if the perp were that dumb?

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:36.810
Don't make me laugh.

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:45.250
The Prime Minister approved your request to use Hozumi as bait.

00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:47.540
But do <i>not</i> let her die.

00:12:47.540 --> 00:12:51.790
She holds numerous state secrets in her un-cyberized regions.

00:12:52.270 --> 00:12:53.380
I'm aware.

00:12:53.380 --> 00:12:56.250
We've prepped the hospital area.

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:59.700
I've done all an "observer" can.

00:12:59.700 --> 00:13:03.670
Major, I found out who Murasaka was tailing.

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:06.640
An upstanding citizen volunteered the info.

00:13:07.070 --> 00:13:12.800
He was apparently after a cyber-drug dealer by the name of Galvez Garcia.

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:14.810
Is he Pyromaniac?

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:16.110
Dunno.

00:13:16.110 --> 00:13:20.830
But Murasaka dropped off the map
 right after attempting contact with him.

00:13:21.830 --> 00:13:23.570
That's all I got here.

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:24.850
I'll keep digging.

00:13:24.850 --> 00:13:25.890
Good.

00:13:27.270 --> 00:13:28.480
This guy, eh?

00:13:49.080 --> 00:13:51.640
Saito!

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:55.020
I made sure all the snipers are in position!

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:07.360
{=0}Department of Cyberbrain Neurology

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:15.300
I'm seeing delays in your storage cells.

00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:19.970
Why don't I prescribe some medicinal micromachines to slow the cyberbrain sclerosis's progression?

00:14:23.600 --> 00:14:25.890
We'll begin the transfer in twenty minutes.

00:14:27.150 --> 00:14:29.560
Your security arrangements are watertight.

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:34.020
They'd be even better if we were in charge.

00:14:34.490 --> 00:14:36.320
That's not going to happen.

00:14:38.550 --> 00:14:41.940
Now it's a matter of whether our prey walks into our trap.

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:47.910
American spires and super-class-A hackers—what reliable escorts.

00:14:48.230 --> 00:14:52.590
We're not doing this for you. This is for us.

00:14:52.590 --> 00:14:55.570
I'm cutting you off from all Nets for a while.

00:14:56.830 --> 00:14:58.650
I'll get a good night's sleep.

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:01.930
What is this?

00:15:01.930 --> 00:15:02.760
Cyberbrain contamination!

00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:04.040
What?

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:05.210
It's him.

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:08.170
He's gotten in.

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:09.630
Batou!

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:12.090
He hasn't tripped any warnings here!

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:18.690
Who <i>is</i> this guy?

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:31.690
Hey.

00:15:32.650 --> 00:15:34.520
What's wrong? Are you okay?

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:35.910
Hey!

00:15:42.020 --> 00:15:42.990
Shit!

00:15:43.870 --> 00:15:45.470
This again?!

00:15:58.400 --> 00:15:59.620
A hacking?!

00:16:02.550 --> 00:16:05.530
The Army's encrypted channel is being hacked!

00:16:08.270 --> 00:16:10.860
Cut the connection, or everyone's brains will be fried!

00:16:11.120 --> 00:16:13.150
I can't! It's locked—

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:25.800
Is Hozumi all right?

00:16:26.530 --> 00:16:29.550
You can't pierce a titanium braincase with a 9mm.

00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:33.720
What do you intend to do?

00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:37.760
Connect you to the Net, using myself as a bypass.

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:38.740
Major!

00:16:38.740 --> 00:16:41.730
I told you: she's my bait.

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:44.850
We'll lure Pyromaniac in and capture him.

00:16:53.590 --> 00:16:56.370
Failure is unacceptable. Make it work.

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:05.470
Ishikawa!

00:17:05.990 --> 00:17:08.850
Access my cyberbrain <i>now</i>.

00:17:08.850 --> 00:17:09.930
We have a job to do.

00:17:10.890 --> 00:17:14.210
A rough one, too, if you're talking like that.

00:17:21.700 --> 00:17:23.610
Use Hozumi as a decoy?!

00:17:23.610 --> 00:17:26.350
Ape-Face is gonna throttle you.

00:17:26.710 --> 00:17:28.210
I got permission.

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:39.830
Pyromaniac should come to fry Hozumi's brain the second we connect her to the Net.

00:17:40.540 --> 00:17:44.940
When he tries to access her, 
keep her guarded and tie down his lines.

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:48.570
While he's distracted, I'll run a trace and pinpoint his location.

00:17:49.240 --> 00:17:51.010
You make it sound so easy.

00:17:51.510 --> 00:17:52.210
Major!

00:17:52.210 --> 00:17:52.740
Major!

00:17:52.740 --> 00:17:54.220
You called and we came!

00:17:54.220 --> 00:17:55.370
Yay!

00:17:55.370 --> 00:17:56.380
We're starting now.

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:57.520
Okay!

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:07.280
Wow, amazing processing speed!

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:09.370
Attack barrier being hacked.

00:18:09.370 --> 00:18:10.950
Gotta restore it!

00:18:11.860 --> 00:18:16.400
You are the greatest sinner here.

00:18:17.010 --> 00:18:20.050
You are the true servant of the Devil.

00:18:20.050 --> 00:18:23.370
<i>Quotes from Bryusov's </i>The Fiery Angel<i>?</i>

00:18:24.800 --> 00:18:26.340
I tied down his lines.

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:29.790
Let all be cast into the flames.

00:18:30.820 --> 00:18:31.890
<i>You're not getting away!</i>

00:18:34.100 --> 00:18:35.340
Major?!

00:18:36.140 --> 00:18:38.300
Did he whiteout?

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:40.340
Does that mean he's dead?

00:18:42.480 --> 00:18:45.060
Concentrate on your work! Time to initialize!

00:18:48.030 --> 00:18:50.400
He packs too many punches! What's going on here?!

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:53.960
He must be using the soldiers' cyberbrains to clone the virus.

00:19:00.350 --> 00:19:01.450
What the heck?

00:19:04.510 --> 00:19:08.320
Logicomas, one of you synchronize with my Net.

00:19:08.320 --> 00:19:10.710
We'll clone his virus and counterattack.

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:11.720
Huh?!

00:19:11.720 --> 00:19:15.810
But that will halve our processing power...

00:19:15.810 --> 00:19:16.680
Just do it!

00:19:16.680 --> 00:19:17.870
Right!

00:19:17.870 --> 00:19:18.680
Oh, dear.

00:19:19.480 --> 00:19:21.130
Pardon me!

00:19:22.940 --> 00:19:25.890
Major, his transfer speed...

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:31.730
Yes. Pyromaniac is hacking us
 from somewhere in this building.

00:19:33.510 --> 00:19:35.740
I don't want to burden my lines.

00:19:35.740 --> 00:19:38.500
Chief, call Batou and Togusa over here.

00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:42.930
Have them search the building until I pinpoint his location.

00:19:42.930 --> 00:19:43.920
All right.

00:20:08.510 --> 00:20:11.020
<i>Where are you, Pyromaniac?</i>

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:14.690
Major! The barrier can't take any more!

00:20:14.690 --> 00:20:16.480
We're almost there. Hold out.

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:26.790
<i>Found him!</i>

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:29.910
Major?!

00:20:37.820 --> 00:20:38.920
Police!

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:41.080
Don't move!

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:03.780
Yes, the deal's come off as planned.

00:21:05.510 --> 00:21:08.290
This is the key to the Third World.

00:21:09.090 --> 00:21:09.750
Drive.

00:21:16.410 --> 00:21:20.710
They say he was driven by layer upon overwritten layer of false memories.

00:21:21.690 --> 00:21:29.080
We didn't find any evidence tying him to the virus' creator,
 nor did we find Fire-Starter's original code.

00:21:29.080 --> 00:21:33.180
He erased the source along with himself—
or rather, someone else did?

00:21:33.690 --> 00:21:38.580
Unconfirmed. We'll have to wait for the specialists' analysis.

00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:48.620
When I accessed that man directly, I didn't sense a Ghost.

00:21:49.670 --> 00:21:55.150
Fire-Starter will spark the evolution of all men's Ghosts.

00:21:55.150 --> 00:21:58.040
Therefore, it must be protected.

00:22:00.590 --> 00:22:06.800
It must use cyberbrains to upgrade, and then be returned to the Net.

00:22:07.430 --> 00:22:11.330
I will go on living even after my death.

00:22:17.270 --> 00:22:19.830
The original Fire-Starter...

00:22:22.370 --> 00:22:24.690
I <i>will</i> track it down.
